component SchedulingAndRecurrence {
    goal {
        Manage recurring booking patterns, their dated series, and exceptions so a
        renter can request repeating room bookings without creating each occurrence
        separately.
    }

    interface {
        A *recurring booking pattern* describes a local start time, duration,
        recurrence rule, and date range.

        Scheduling and Recurrence expands a valid recurring booking pattern into a
        *recurring booking series* of dated occurrences.

        A user can add a *series exception* to skip or move one occurrence without
        changing the other occurrences in that series.

        Expanding a local-time pattern across clock changes requires
        *regional time-zone rules*.
    }

    state {
        Scheduling and Recurrence owns the recurring booking pattern, recurring
        booking series, and series exception.

        A recurring booking series links one pattern to its dated occurrences.

        A series exception applies to one occurrence in its recurring booking series.
    }

    logic {
        Scheduling and Recurrence validates a requested recurring booking pattern.
        If the pattern is rejected, it returns a validation result and ends that path.

        For an accepted pattern, Scheduling and Recurrence expands the pattern into
        dated occurrences.

        It applies each series exception to the matching dated occurrence to produce
        the adjusted occurrence set.

        It returns the recurring booking series containing the accepted pattern and
        adjusted occurrence set.

        Separately, it builds a *series-date preview* from the recurring booking
        pattern for the booking form.
    }

    constraints {
        Resource Management owns base room availability. Expanding a series does not
        decide whether its occurrences are bookable for a room.

        Identity and Access decides whether a user may create or change a series.
        Scheduling and Recurrence does not own users, sessions, roles, or permission
        policy.

        Modules exchange contracts and do not read another module's private storage
        or logic.
    }

    cases {
        A renter requests a weekly room booking across four weeks and skips one date;
        only that occurrence is omitted from the recurring booking series.
    }
}
